/-!
# The flow near a rest point

Let `v` be a vector field on a boundaryless manifold modelled on a Banach space and `p` a rest
point, `v p = 0`. The trajectory through `p` is constant, so `p` lies in the flow domain at every
time and every time-`t` map of the flow fixes it (`TauCeti.flowOf_eq_self_of_eq_zero`). The
differentials `dφ_t(p) : T_p M → T_p M` of these maps form a one-parameter family of operators on
the single tangent space `T_p M`.

Read `v` in the preferred chart at `p`, as the inverse-chart pullback
`V = VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm v (range I)`. Its derivative
`L = DV` at the chart image of `p` is the linearization of `v` at the rest point. For a `C²` field
the family `dφ_t(p)` has derivative `L` at `t = 0`
(`TauCeti.hasDerivAt_mfderiv_flowOf_of_eq_zero`), so `dφ_t(p) = 1 + t L + o(t)`. The flow is
jointly `C²`, so in the chart it is a `C²` function `Ψ(t, z)` of time and position whose time
derivative at `t = 0` is `V`; the symmetry of its second derivative exchanges the time derivative
of the spatial derivative `D_z Ψ (t, ·)` with the spatial derivative `DV` of the time derivative.

Consequently, if the model space is finite-dimensional and `L` is injective, then for `t ≠ 0` close
to `0` the rest point is a nondegenerate fixed point of the time-`t` map
(`TauCeti.eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf`): `1` is not an eigenvalue of `dφ_t(p)`. For
the Hamiltonian vector field of a Morse function this makes the critical points nondegenerate
constant orbits of `ε F` for small `ε > 0`.

The same holds for a `C²` time-dependent field `X` on a finite-dimensional manifold vanishing at
`p` at all times. Every time map `φ_{s,t}` of its flow fixes `p`, and with `L_t` the derivative
of the coordinate expression of `X t` at the chart image of `p`, the differentials solve the
linear equation `∂ₜ dφ_{s,t}(p) = L_t ∘ dφ_{s,t}(p)`
(`TauCeti.hasDerivAt_mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_of_forall_eq_zero`). The time-`t` derivative of
the flow from time `t` is computed as in the autonomous case, and the flow from time `s` factors
near `p` through time `t`. Consequently, if `X u` vanishes to first order at `p`, that is `L_u = 0`,
for every time `u` between `s` and `t`, then `dφ_{s,t}(p)` is the identity
(`TauCeti.mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_eq_id_of_forall_eq_zero`). Applied at every point of a
submanifold, this shows that an isotopy generated by a field vanishing to first order along the
submanifold, such as a Moser isotopy built from a primitive with zero first jet there, has
differential the identity on the full ambient tangent spaces along it.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.mem_flowDomain_of_eq_zero`, `TauCeti.flowOf_eq_self_of_eq_zero`: the flow is defined at
  a rest point for all time and fixes it.
* `TauCeti.mdifferentiableAt_flowOf_of_eq_zero`: the time-`t` maps are differentiable at a rest
  point.
* `TauCeti.hasDerivAt_mfderiv_flowOf_of_eq_zero`: the differentials of the time-`t` maps at a rest
  point have derivative the linearization of the field at `t = 0`.
* `TauCeti.eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf`: on a finite-dimensional manifold, a rest
  point with injective linearization is a nondegenerate fixed point of the time-`t` maps for small
  `t ≠ 0`.
* `TauCeti.hasDerivAt_mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_of_forall_eq_zero`: at a common rest point of a
  time-dependent field, the differentials of the time maps solve the linearized equation.
* `TauCeti.mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_eq_id_of_forall_eq_zero`: if moreover the linearizations
  vanish between the two times, the differential of the time map is the identity.

## References

* M. W. Hirsch, S. Smale, R. L. Devaney, *Differential Equations, Dynamical Systems, and an
  Introduction to Chaos*, 3rd ed., Academic Press, 2013, Chapter 8 (linearization at
  equilibria).
-/

public section

open Filter Function Set
open scoped Manifold Topology ContDiff

namespace TauCeti

variable {E H M : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]
  {v : (x : M) → TangentSpace I x} {p : M}

/-- **The flow is defined at a rest point for all time.** -/
theorem mem_flowDomain_of_eq_zero (hp : v p = 0) (t : ℝ) : (t, p) ∈ flowDomain v :=
  mem_flowDomain.2 ((isMIntegralCurve_const hp).maximalIntegralCurveInterval_eq_univ rfl ▸
    mem_univ t)

variable [T2Space M]

/-- **The flow fixes a rest point.** Every time-`t` map of the flow of a `C¹` field fixes a point
at which the field vanishes. -/
theorem flowOf_eq_self_of_eq_zero [IsManifold I 1 M] [BoundarylessManifold I M]
    (hv : CMDiff 1 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, v y⟩ : TangentBundle I M))) (hp : v p = 0) (t : ℝ) :
    flowOf v t p = p :=
  flowOf_eq_of_isMIntegralCurve hv (isMIntegralCurve_const hp) t

/-- **The time-`t` maps of the flow are differentiable at a rest point.** For a `C¹` field `v` on a
boundaryless manifold modelled on a Banach space, every time-`t` map of the flow is differentiable
at a point where `v` vanishes. -/
theorem mdifferentiableAt_flowOf_of_eq_zero [CompleteSpace E] [IsManifold I 1 M]
    [BoundarylessManifold I M] (hv : CMDiff 1 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, v y⟩ : TangentBundle I M)))
    (hp : v p = 0) (t : ℝ) : MDifferentiableAt I I (flowOf v t) p :=
  (contMDiffAt_flowOf_comp le_rfl hv contMDiffAt_const contMDiffAt_id
    (mem_flowDomain_of_eq_zero hp t)).mdifferentiableAt one_ne_zero

variable [CompleteSpace E] [I.Boundaryless] [IsManifold I 2 M]

/-- **Linearization of the flow at a rest point.** For a `C²` vector field `v` vanishing at `p`, the
differentials `dφ_t(p) : T_p M → T_p M` of the time-`t` maps of the flow have derivative at
`t = 0` the derivative `L` of the coordinate expression of `v` in the preferred chart at `p`, so
`dφ_t(p) = 1 + t L + o(t)`. -/
theorem hasDerivAt_mfderiv_flowOf_of_eq_zero
    (hv : CMDiff 2 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, v y⟩ : TangentBundle I M))) (hp : v p = 0) :
    HasDerivAt (fun t ↦ (mfderiv I I (flowOf v t) p : E →L[ℝ] E))
      (fderiv ℝ (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm v (range I))
        (extChartAt I p p)) 0 := by
  have hv1 : CMDiff 1 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, v y⟩ : TangentBundle I M)) := hv.of_le one_le_two
  -- In the preferred chart at `p`, the flow is a jointly `C²` family fixing `p` at time `0`.
  have hG := Manifold.contDiffAt_extChartAt_family (flowOf_zero v p)
    ((contMDiffOn_flowOf one_le_two hv).contMDiffAt
      ((isOpen_flowDomain hv1).mem_nhds (mem_flowDomain_zero hv1 p)))
  -- In the chart, the trajectories start with the coordinate velocity of `v`.
  have hV := eventually_hasDerivAt_extChartAt_family (ψ := fun u x ↦ flowOf v u x) (V := v)
    (t := 0) (y := p) (Eventually.of_forall fun x ↦ flowOf_zero v x)
    (Eventually.of_forall fun x ↦
      ((isMIntegralCurveOn_flowOf hv1 x).isMIntegralCurveAt
        (((isOpen_flowDomain hv1).preimage (continuous_id.prodMk continuous_const)).mem_nhds
          (mem_flowDomain_zero hv1 x))).hasMFDerivAt)
  refine (ContDiffAt.hasDerivAt_fderiv_slice_of_eventually_hasDerivAt
      (by rw [minSmoothness_of_isRCLikeNormedField]; exact_mod_cast hG) hV)
    |>.congr_of_eventuallyEq (Eventually.of_forall fun t ↦ ?_)
  -- Each time-`t` map fixes `p`, so its differential is read in the single chart at `p`.
  exact (mdifferentiableAt_flowOf_of_eq_zero hv1 hp t).mfderiv_eq_fderiv_extChartAt_conj
    (flowOf_eq_self_of_eq_zero hv1 hp t)

/-- **A rest point with injective linearization is a nondegenerate fixed point of the short-time
maps.** On a boundaryless manifold modelled on a finite-dimensional space, let `v` be a `C²` vector
field vanishing at `p` whose coordinate expression in the preferred chart at `p` has injective
derivative at the chart image of `p`. Then for every `t ≠ 0`
close to `0`, the point `p` is a nondegenerate fixed point of the time-`t` map of the flow. -/
theorem eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    (hv : CMDiff 2 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, v y⟩ : TangentBundle I M))) (hp : v p = 0)
    (hL : Injective (fderiv ℝ
      (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm v (range I))
        (extChartAt I p p))) :
    ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝[≠] 0, IsNondegenerateFixedPt I (flowOf v t) p := by
  have hv1 : CMDiff 1 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, v y⟩ : TangentBundle I M)) := hv.of_le one_le_two
  have hid : flowOf v 0 = id := funext (flowOf_zero v)
  -- `mfderiv_id` is the identity of `TangentSpace I p`, which is `E` by definition.
  have h0 : (mfderiv I I (flowOf v 0) p : E →L[ℝ] E) = ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ E := by
    rw [hid, mfderiv_id]
    rfl
  filter_upwards [(hasDerivAt_mfderiv_flowOf_of_eq_zero hv hp).eventually_eq_zero_of_apply_eq_self
    (E := E) (A := fun t ↦ (mfderiv I I (flowOf v t) p : E →L[ℝ] E)) h0 hL] with t ht
  -- `ht` is about vectors of `E`, which are the tangent vectors at `p` by definition.
  exact isNondegenerateFixedPt_iff.2 ⟨flowOf_eq_self_of_eq_zero hv1 hp t,
    mdifferentiableAt_flowOf_of_eq_zero hv1 hp t, ht⟩

/-! ### Time-dependent flows -/

section TimeDependent

omit [CompleteSpace E]

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {X : ℝ → (x : M) → TangentSpace I x}

/-- At a rest point `p` of a `C²` time-dependent field `X`, the differentials of the flow from
time `t` have derivative at time `t` the linearization of `X t` at `p`, read in the preferred
chart at `p`. -/
private theorem hasDerivAt_mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_self_of_forall_eq_zero
    (hX : ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod I) I.tangent 2
      (fun q : ℝ × M ↦ (⟨q.2, X q.1 q.2⟩ : TangentBundle I M)))
    (hp : ∀ u, X u p = 0) (t : ℝ) :
    HasDerivAt (F := E →L[ℝ] E) (fun u ↦ mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X t u) p)
      (fderiv ℝ (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm (X t) (range I))
        (extChartAt I p p)) t := by
  have hX₁ := hX.of_le one_le_two
  -- The flow from time `t` is jointly `C²` in the final time and the point near `(t, p)`.
  have hψ : ContMDiffAt (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod I) I 2
      (Function.uncurry fun u y ↦ timeDependentFlowOf X t u y) (t, p) :=
    ((contMDiffOn_timeDependentFlowOf (n := 2) (by norm_num) hX).contMDiffAt
      ((isOpen_timeDependentFlowDomain hX₁).mem_nhds
        (mem_timeDependentFlowDomain_self hX₁ t p))).comp
          (t, p) ((contMDiffAt_const.prodMk contMDiffAt_fst).prodMk contMDiffAt_snd)
  have hG := Manifold.contDiffAt_extChartAt_family (timeDependentFlowOf_self X t p) hψ
  -- In the chart, the trajectories start at time `t` with the coordinate velocity of `X t`.
  have hV := eventually_hasDerivAt_extChartAt_family
    (ψ := fun u y ↦ timeDependentFlowOf X t u y) (V := X t) (t := t) (y := p)
    (Eventually.of_forall fun x ↦ timeDependentFlowOf_self X t x)
    (Eventually.of_forall fun x ↦
      hasMFDerivAt_timeDependentFlowOf hX₁ (mem_timeDependentFlowDomain_self hX₁ t x))
  refine (ContDiffAt.hasDerivAt_fderiv_slice_of_eventually_hasDerivAt
      (by rw [minSmoothness_of_isRCLikeNormedField]; exact_mod_cast hG) hV)
    |>.congr_of_eventuallyEq (Eventually.of_forall fun u ↦ ?_)
  -- Each time map fixes `p`, so its differential is read in the single chart at `p`.
  exact (mdifferentiableAt_timeDependentFlowOf hX₁
    (mem_timeDependentFlowDomain_of_forall_eq_zero hp t u)).mfderiv_eq_fderiv_extChartAt_conj
      (timeDependentFlowOf_eq_self_of_forall_eq_zero hX₁ hp t u)

/-- **Linearization of a time-dependent flow at a rest point.** Let `X` be a `C²` time-dependent
vector field on a boundaryless finite-dimensional manifold, vanishing at `p` at all times, so
that every time map `φ_{s,t}` of its flow fixes `p`. Then the differentials
`dφ_{s,t}(p) : T_p M → T_p M` solve the linear equation `∂ₜ dφ_{s,t}(p) = L_t ∘ dφ_{s,t}(p)`,
where `L_t` is the derivative at the chart image of `p` of the coordinate expression of `X t` in
the preferred chart at `p`, the linearization of `X t` at its zero `p`. -/
theorem hasDerivAt_mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_of_forall_eq_zero
    (hX : ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod I) I.tangent 2
      (fun q : ℝ × M ↦ (⟨q.2, X q.1 q.2⟩ : TangentBundle I M)))
    (hp : ∀ u, X u p = 0) (s t : ℝ) :
    HasDerivAt (F := E →L[ℝ] E) (fun u ↦ mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X s u) p)
      ((fderiv ℝ (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm (X t) (range I))
        (extChartAt I p p)).comp (mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X s t) p)) t := by
  have hX₁ := hX.of_le one_le_two
  have hdom := isOpen_timeDependentFlowDomain hX₁
  have hst := mem_timeDependentFlowDomain_of_forall_eq_zero hp s t
  have hpt := timeDependentFlowOf_eq_self_of_forall_eq_zero hX₁ hp s t
  have hf := mdifferentiableAt_timeDependentFlowOf hX₁ hst
  -- Near `(t, p)`, flowing from `s` to `t` and then from `t` to `u` is defined.
  have hS : ∀ᶠ q : ℝ × M in 𝓝 (t, p), ((s, t), q.2) ∈ timeDependentFlowDomain X ∧
      ((t, q.1), timeDependentFlowOf X s t q.2) ∈ timeDependentFlowDomain X := by
    refine Eventually.and ?_ ?_
    · exact ContinuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds (f := fun q : ℝ × M ↦ ((s, t), q.2))
        ((continuous_const.prodMk continuous_id).continuousAt.comp continuousAt_snd)
        (hdom.mem_nhds hst)
    · refine ContinuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds
        (f := fun q : ℝ × M ↦ ((t, q.1), timeDependentFlowOf X s t q.2)) ?_ (hdom.mem_nhds ?_)
      · exact (continuousAt_const.prodMk continuousAt_fst).prodMk
          (hf.continuousAt.comp continuousAt_snd)
      · simpa only [hpt] using mem_timeDependentFlowDomain_self hX₁ t p
  rw [nhds_prod_eq] at hS
  set A : ℝ → E →L[ℝ] E := fun u ↦ mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X t u) p
  set B : E →L[ℝ] E := mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X s t) p
  have hA₀ : HasDerivAt A _ t :=
    hasDerivAt_mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_self_of_forall_eq_zero hX hp t
  have hA := hA₀.clm_comp (hasDerivAt_const t B)
  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_zero, add_zero] at hA
  refine hA.congr_of_eventuallyEq ?_
  filter_upwards [hS.curry] with u hu
  -- The flow from `s` to `u` agrees near `p` with the composite through time `t`.
  have hcomp : timeDependentFlowOf X t u ∘ timeDependentFlowOf X s t =ᶠ[𝓝 p]
      timeDependentFlowOf X s u :=
    hu.mono fun y hy ↦ (timeDependentFlowOf_trans_of_mem hX₁ hy.1 hy.2).2
  have hg := (mdifferentiableAt_timeDependentFlowOf hX₁
    (mem_timeDependentFlowDomain_of_forall_eq_zero hp t u)).hasMFDerivAt
  rw [← hpt] at hg
  exact ((hg.comp p hf.hasMFDerivAt).congr_of_eventuallyEq_abuse hcomp.symm).mfderiv.trans
    (by rw [hpt]; rfl)

/-- **A time-dependent flow fixes a rest point to first order where the linearization
vanishes.** Let `X` be a `C²` time-dependent vector field on a boundaryless finite-dimensional
manifold, vanishing at `p` at all times. If the linearization of `X u` at `p`, read in the
preferred chart at `p`, vanishes for every time `u` between `s` and `t`, then the differential of
the time map `φ_{s,t}` at `p` is the identity. -/
theorem mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_eq_id_of_forall_eq_zero
    (hX : ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod I) I.tangent 2
      (fun q : ℝ × M ↦ (⟨q.2, X q.1 q.2⟩ : TangentBundle I M)))
    (hp : ∀ u, X u p = 0) {s t : ℝ}
    (hL : ∀ u ∈ uIcc s t, fderiv ℝ
      (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm (X u) (range I))
        (extChartAt I p p) = 0) :
    mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X s t) p = ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ (TangentSpace I p) := by
  set W : ℝ → E →L[ℝ] E := fun u ↦ mfderiv I I (timeDependentFlowOf X s u) p
  have hW (u : ℝ) : HasDerivAt (F := E →L[ℝ] E) W ((fderiv ℝ
      (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm (X u) (range I))
        (extChartAt I p p)).comp (W u)) u :=
    hasDerivAt_mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_of_forall_eq_zero hX hp s u
  -- `W` has zero derivative between `s` and `t`, so it is constant there.
  have hconst := constant_of_has_deriv_right_zero (a := min s t) (b := max s t) (f := W)
    (fun u _ ↦ (hW u).continuousAt.continuousWithinAt) fun u hu ↦ by
      have h := (hW u).hasDerivWithinAt (s := Ici u)
      rwa [hL u (Ico_subset_Icc_self hu), ContinuousLinearMap.zero_comp] at h
  have hs : W s = W (min s t) := hconst s ⟨min_le_left s t, le_max_left s t⟩
  have ht : W t = W (min s t) := hconst t ⟨min_le_right s t, le_max_right s t⟩
  have hid : W s = ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ E := mfderiv_timeDependentFlowOf_self X s p
  exact (ht.trans hs.symm).trans hid

end TimeDependent

end TauCeti
